Chase Torre
UHCL Senior Project II Spring 2026



--DESCRIPTION--

The two listed .stl's are the 3D models I created for 3D printing both the Arduino Nano 33 Iot and mini breadboard housing.
I wanted to create easy access to both the MCU and the breadboard, so I created housings that can be threaded onto the glove itself, 
along with 0.2 mm tolerance lids for a snug fit. The housings themselves are very durable, with a 2 mm thickness at 25% infill. 



--Current Features--

- Both housings are made out of black PLA basic, and printed on a Flashforge Adventurer 5M Pro using the Orca-Flashforge slicer. 
- Outer holes, with a 3 mm diameter, to allow for threading the housings onto the glove.
- Velcro mounts for MCU and breadboard (in progress) 
- Two cutouts for the breadboard shell, for connections to the MCU and flex sensors.
- Four cutouts for the Nano shell, one for USB access, and the rest for connections to the breadboard.


